{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TyKeGi7NjddzmoGe9GEKKp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd011-magefiles\n     2→title: \"magefiles and cmd/version: Build Lifecycle and Version Identity\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  go-unix-utils has no testable artifact until its first utility passes differential tests.\n     6→  The mage build targets (build, lint, clean, install) are inherited from cobbler-scaffold's\n     7→  orchestrator library, but the project has no specification for what those targets must do\n     8→  in this repository. Without a PRD the build lifecycle is an undocumented dependency of\n     9→  every other PRD.\n    10→\n    11→  A second gap is version identity. The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N)\n    12→  and code releases (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n    13→  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete, testable\n    14→  artifact that exercises the full build pipeline (compile, lint, test, install) before any\n    15→  utility code exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n    16→  when they need to report their own version.\n    17→\n    18→goals:\n    19→  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n    20→  - G2: Specify the build target that compiles all cmd/ binaries to bin/.\n    21→  - G3: Specify the lint target that runs golangci-lint on all Go source.\n    22→  - G4: Specify the clean target that removes build artifacts.\n    23→  - G5: Specify the install target that runs go install for cmd/ binaries.\n    24→  - G6: Specify the configuration contract between magefiles/ and configuration.yaml for the fields consumed by these targets.\n    25→\n    26→requirements:\n    27→  R1:\n    28→    title: cmd/version binary\n    29→    items:\n    30→      - R1.1: |\n    31→          Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n    32→          invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n    33→          by a newline and exits 0.\n    34→      - R1.2: |\n    35→          The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n    36→          When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n    37→          \"dev\" as the version string.\n    38→      - R1.3: |\n    39→          The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n    40→          git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n    41→          linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n    42→          succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n    43→      - R1.4: |\n    44→          When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n    45→          as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n    46→          usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n    47→      - R1.5: |\n    48→          The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n    49→          can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n    50→          mechanism.\n    51→\n    52→  R2:\n    53→    title: Build target\n    54→    items:\n    55→      - R2.1: |\n    56→          mage build must compile every package under cmd/ to a binary in the directory\n    57→          specified by configuration.yaml project.binary_dir (default: bin/). Each binary\n    58→          is named after its cmd/ subdirectory (e.g., cmd/version/ produces bin/version).\n    59→      - R2.2: |\n    60→          mage build must pass -ldflags with the version tag resolved per R1.3 to every\n    61→          cmd/ binary that imports the version variable.\n    62→      - R2.3: |\n    63→          mage build must fail with a non-zero exit code if any cmd/ package fails to\n    64→          compile. The error message must identify which package failed.\n    65→      - R2.4: |\n    66→          mage build must create the binary_dir if it does not exist.\n    67→\n    68→  R3:\n    69→    title: Lint target\n    70→    items:\n    71→      - R3.1: |\n    72→          mage lint must run golangci-lint on all Go source directories listed in\n    73→          configuration.yaml project.go_source_dirs (default: pkg, cmd). The linter\n    74→          must also cover magefiles/.\n    75→      - R3.2: |\n    76→          mage lint must fail with a non-zero exit code if golangci-lint reports any\n    77→          warnings or errors.\n    78→      - R3.3: |\n    79→          The golangci-lint configuration must be committed to the repository (as\n    80→          .golangci.yml or equivalent) so that lint results are reproducible.\n    81→\n    82→  R4:\n    83→    title: Clean target\n    84→    items:\n    85→      - R4.1: |\n    86→          mage clean must remove the binary_dir and all its contents. If the directory\n    87→          does not exist, the target must succeed silently.\n    88→      - R4.2: |\n    89→          mage clean must not remove source files, documentation, or any directory\n    90→          outside binary_dir.\n    91→\n    92→  R5:\n    93→    title: Install target\n    94→    items:\n    95→      - R5.1: |\n    96→          mage install must run go install for every package under cmd/, installing\n    97→          binaries to the Go bin directory ($GOPATH/bin or $GOBIN).\n    98→      - R5.2: |\n    99→          mage install must pass the same -ldflags as mage build (R2.2).\n   100→\n   101→  R6:\n   102→    title: Configuration contract\n   103→    items:\n   104→      - R6.1: |\n   105→          The following fields in configuration.yaml project section are consumed by the\n   106→          build lifecycle targets and must be present:\n   107→\n   108→            project.module_path    — Go module path (used by go build)\n   109→            project.binary_dir     — output directory for compiled binaries (default: bin)\n   110→            project.go_source_dirs — list of directories containing Go source (default: [pkg, cmd])\n   111→            project.magefiles_dir  — directory containing mage targets (default: magefiles)\n   112→      - R6.2: |\n   113→          magefiles/orchestrator.go must load configuration.yaml at init time via the\n   114→          orchestrator library. If the file does not exist, the init function must create\n   115→          a default configuration file and log the action to stderr.\n   116→      - R6.3: |\n   117→          Build lifecycle targets (build, lint, clean, install) must not depend on fields\n   118→          outside the project section of configuration.yaml. Orchestrator, cobbler, and\n   119→          claude sections are consumed by cobbler-scaffold targets, not by this PRD's scope.\n   120→\n   121→non_goals:\n   122→  - This PRD does not specify orchestrator targets (cobbler:measure, cobbler:stitch). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   123→  - This PRD does not specify generator lifecycle targets (generator:start, generator:run, generator:stop). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   124→  - This PRD does not specify scaffold, prompt, or stats targets. Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   125→  - This PRD does not specify the analyze target. Cross-artifact consistency checks are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n   126→  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n   127→\n   128→acceptance_criteria:\n   129→  - \"AC1: mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n   130→  - \"AC2: bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n   131→  - \"AC3: bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n   132→  - \"AC4: A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n   133→  - \"AC5: mage lint runs golangci-lint on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with no warnings.\"\n   134→  - \"AC6: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds silently when bin/ does not exist.\"\n   135→  - \"AC7: mage build followed by mage clean followed by ls bin/ shows bin/ does not exist.\"\n   136→  - \"AC8: All configuration fields consumed by build lifecycle targets are documented in R6.1 and present in configuration.yaml.\"\n   137→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55d946ae-dfe8-486f-8a89-44582e2a8d3b","uuid":"d59c9997-2ea5-48da-a375-92680a2edc28","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/104/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd011-magefiles.yaml","content":"id: prd011-magefiles\ntitle: \"magefiles and cmd/version: Build Lifecycle and Version Identity\"\n\nproblem: |\n  go-unix-utils has no testable artifact until its first utility passes differential tests.\n  The mage build targets (build, lint, clean, install) are inherited from cobbler-scaffold's\n  orchestrator library, but the project has no specification for what those targets must do\n  in this repository. Without a PRD the build lifecycle is an undocumented dependency of\n  every other PRD.\n\n  A second gap is version identity. The project tags documentation releases (v0.YYYYMMDD.N)\n  and code releases (v1.YYYYMMDD.N), but no binary reports which version it was built from.\n  A cmd/version binary that prints the last known version tag gives a concrete, testable\n  artifact that exercises the full build pipeline (compile, lint, test, install) before any\n  utility code exists. It also provides a version string that other cmd/ binaries can import\n  when they need to report their own version.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Specify a cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag.\n  - G2: Specify the build target that compiles all cmd/ binaries to bin/.\n  - G3: Specify the lint target that runs golangci-lint on all Go source.\n  - G4: Specify the clean target that removes build artifacts.\n  - G5: Specify the install target that runs go install for cmd/ binaries.\n  - G6: Specify the configuration contract between magefiles/ and configuration.yaml for the fields consumed by these targets.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: cmd/version binary\n    items:\n      - R1.1: |\n          Must provide a cmd/version/ package that compiles to a standalone binary. When\n          invoked with no arguments, the binary prints the version string to stdout followed\n          by a newline and exits 0.\n      - R1.2: |\n          The version string must be set at build time via -ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\".\n          When the linker variable is not set (development builds), the binary must print\n          \"dev\" as the version string.\n      - R1.3: |\n          The mage build target must resolve the version tag by running\n          git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passing the result to the\n          linker. If the git command fails (no tags, not a git repository), the build must\n          succeed with the version set to \"dev\".\n      - R1.4: |\n          When invoked with --version or -v, the binary must print the same version string\n          as the no-argument invocation. Any other flag must cause the binary to print a\n          usage message to stderr and exit 2.\n      - R1.5: |\n          The version package must export a variable or function so that other cmd/ packages\n          can import and report the same version string without duplicating the ldflags\n          mechanism.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Build target\n    items:\n      - R2.1: |\n          mage build must compile every package under cmd/ to a binary in the directory\n          specified by configuration.yaml project.binary_dir (default: bin/). Each binary\n          is named after its cmd/ subdirectory (e.g., cmd/version/ produces bin/version).\n      - R2.2: |\n          mage build must pass -ldflags with the version tag resolved per R1.3 to every\n          cmd/ binary that imports the version variable.\n      - R2.3: |\n          mage build must fail with a non-zero exit code if any cmd/ package fails to\n          compile. The error message must identify which package failed.\n      - R2.4: |\n          mage build must create the binary_dir if it does not exist.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Lint target\n    items:\n      - R3.1: |\n          mage lint must run golangci-lint on all Go source directories listed in\n          configuration.yaml project.go_source_dirs (default: pkg, cmd). The linter\n          must also cover magefiles/.\n      - R3.2: |\n          mage lint must fail with a non-zero exit code if golangci-lint reports any\n          warnings or errors.\n      - R3.3: |\n          The golangci-lint configuration must be committed to the repository (as\n          .golangci.yml or equivalent) so that lint results are reproducible.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Clean target\n    items:\n      - R4.1: |\n          mage clean must remove the binary_dir and all its contents. If the directory\n          does not exist, the target must succeed silently.\n      - R4.2: |\n          mage clean must not remove source files, documentation, or any directory\n          outside binary_dir.\n\n  R5:\n    title: Install target\n    items:\n      - R5.1: |\n          mage install must run go install for every package under cmd/, installing\n          binaries to the Go bin directory ($GOPATH/bin or $GOBIN).\n      - R5.2: |\n          mage install must pass the same -ldflags as mage build (R2.2).\n\n  R6:\n    title: Configuration contract\n    items:\n      - R6.1: |\n          The following fields in configuration.yaml project section are consumed by the\n          build lifecycle targets and must be present:\n\n            project.module_path    — Go module path (used by go build)\n            project.binary_dir     — output directory for compiled binaries (default: bin)\n            project.go_source_dirs — list of directories containing Go source (default: [pkg, cmd])\n            project.magefiles_dir  — directory containing mage targets (default: magefiles)\n      - R6.2: |\n          magefiles/orchestrator.go must load configuration.yaml at init time via the\n          orchestrator library. If the file does not exist, the init function must create\n          a default configuration file and log the action to stderr.\n      - R6.3: |\n          Build lifecycle targets (build, lint, clean, install) must not depend on fields\n          outside the project section of configuration.yaml. Orchestrator, cobbler, and\n          claude sections are consumed by cobbler-scaffold targets, not by this PRD's scope.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - This PRD does not specify orchestrator targets (cobbler:measure, cobbler:stitch). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - This PRD does not specify generator lifecycle targets (generator:start, generator:run, generator:stop). Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - This PRD does not specify scaffold, prompt, or stats targets. Those are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - This PRD does not specify the analyze target. Cross-artifact consistency checks are provided by cobbler-scaffold.\n  - cmd/version does not parse LS_COLORS, handle signals, or do anything beyond printing a version string.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: mage build compiles cmd/version/ to bin/version. Running bin/version prints a version tag string (matching v[0-9]*) followed by a newline and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC2: bin/version --version prints the same output as bin/version with no arguments.\"\n  - \"AC3: bin/version --bogus prints a usage message to stderr and exits 2.\"\n  - \"AC4: A development build (without ldflags) produces a binary that prints \\\"dev\\\".\"\n  - \"AC5: mage lint runs golangci-lint on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with no warnings.\"\n  - \"AC6: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds silently when bin/ does not exist.\"\n  - \"AC7: mage build followed by mage clean followed by ls bin/ shows bin/ does not exist.\"\n  - \"AC8: All configuration fields consumed by build lifecycle targets are documented in R6.1 and present in configuration.yaml.\"\n","numLines":137,"startLine":1,"totalLines":137}}}
